<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  accessibilityEventTypes is deliberately narrow: window state changes (app
  switch / new screen), content changes (feed scroll settling, image loads),
  scroll events, and text changes. We do NOT listen for
  typeViewClicked/typeViewFocused/etc - every extra event type is extra
  wakeups on a battery-first design.

  typeViewTextChanged was added specifically for gate 4b (KeywordBlocklist):
  without it, nothing woke onAccessibilityEvent while someone was actively
  typing a search term into an address bar or search box - typing an
  EditText's content fires TYPE_VIEW_TEXT_CHANGED, not
  TYPE_WINDOW_CONTENT_CHANGED, so gate 4b only ever got checked whenever
  recheckStaticContent's periodic backstop next happened to fire (paced to
  the capture-cadence setting, ~2s at the default). A keyword typed and
  submitted faster than that window could slip through uncaught, and even
  when it didn't, the multi-second lag before a block appeared was reported
  as "the keyword blocker is working, but too slowly." Listening for this
  event type directly means gate 4b runs within the ordinary event
  debounce window (~100ms) of each keystroke instead of waiting on the
  backstop - every other gate's behavior is unchanged, since
  onAccessibilityEvent's existing gates (scope, debounce, overlay-visible)
  apply to this event type exactly as they do to the others.

  canRetrieveWindowContent + flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows let
  NodeInspector walk the tree to look for image-bearing nodes before we ever
  touch pixels (gate 3 in the cascade).

  android:canTakeScreenshot is what actually grants CAPABILITY_CAN_TAKE_SCREENSHOT
  for AccessibilityService.takeScreenshot() (API 30+). VERIFY ON-DEVICE: this
  is exactly the kind of flag ColorOS/OEM skins sometimes strip or gate behind
  an extra toggle in their own accessibility/permission UI. If takeScreenshot()
  callbacks fire ERROR_TAKE_SCREENSHOT_INTERNAL_ERROR or similar on the Find X9
  Pro, check Settings > Accessibility > ContentGuard for a ColorOS-specific
  "screenshot" toggle before assuming the API itself is broken.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged|typeViewScrolled|typeViewTextChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:canTakeScreenshot="true"
    android:notificationTimeout="100"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description" />
